<p>In the latest turn, President Trump said Iran must reopen the Strait of Hormuz by Tuesday evening or face US attacks on Iranian power plants and bridges, escalating a confrontation that has become a central flashpoint in the six-week US-Israel war with Iran. Iranian officials rejected the ultimatum and warned that any further escalation could spread across the region, while several outlets reported that Tehran tied any reopening of the strait to broader wartime demands and damages. One of the few brighter notes in an otherwise tense story came from a high-risk US rescue operation inside Iran: after a complex two-day effort, both aviators from the downed F-15 were ultimately recovered. Even so, the rescue and Iran’s downing of the jet seemed to harden positions on both sides rather than open a path to a ceasefire, as shipping through Hormuz remained a global concern because of the waterway’s role in oil and gas trade and Brent crude rose slightly above $110 a barrel.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JeRXfN8P_U7IFhEyaFoGLC2wMKF0K0csJ3fMZrQFlDnY94Ww-sX8mBKwKZhK4WheWdH5r0r81ZwTvqmKQRt4dVaU9AN6DMSOtvfsA-kv4Y0ezFZeg0SlVSg-tY0gyg6dqsGc1H6ElUsr-LzfSRSrz-btheQwF8afqKuk-dcLnBt6QgQfbi_WvWTo9CJbNVt0lRtGaQs6hqAOzNAysqjuB2Tsg2oHR56SpgPEpGmTYzjvQRCXuhI' alt='Boats in the Strait of Hormuz in March. Transit through the waterway has slowed to a trickle since the start of the conflict.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Exact cutoff: Mercopress reported that Trump set the ultimatum for Tuesday at 8:00 PM Eastern Time, giving the threat a precise public deadline instead of a general Tuesday warning.</li><li>Religious framing: Reuters-based reporting said Trump and other U.S. officials described the rescue as an &#x27;Easter miracle&#x27;, drawing criticism that religious language was being used to frame the war effort.</li><li>US criticism: Democratic lawmakers including Chuck Schumer, Chris Murphy and Tim Kaine publicly criticized President Trump’s language and warned about the legal and strategic consequences of threatening civilian infrastructure.</li><li>Regional strikes: As diplomacy stalled, Reuters-based reporting cited by Dawn said Iran’s Revolutionary Guards struck a petrochemical facility in Israel while US strikes hit Ahvaz airport, underscoring the conflict’s widening military scope.</li><li>Propaganda vs. caution: The Guardian argued that recovering the downed F-15 crew may hand Trump a propaganda win, but it also shows that Iran can still impose real military costs on the United States.</li></ul><blockquote>Our whole region is going to burn - Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump said he still saw &quot;a good chance&quot; of a deal even as he warned that, if Iran did not act quickly, he was considering destroying infrastructure and taking over the oil. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-threatens-to-hit-irans-infrastructure-on-tuesday-if-strait-of-hormuz-remains-blocked/article70826992.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iranian mission to the UN: Iran’s UN mission said the threat to hit power plants and bridges was clear evidence of intent to commit a war crime and called on the international community to prevent it. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988918/strait-of-hormuz-stays-sticking-point-as-ceasefire-remains-elusive'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Russia: Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov urged Washington to drop what he called the language of ultimatums and joined calls for a ceasefire. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988918/strait-of-hormuz-stays-sticking-point-as-ceasefire-remains-elusive'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistan said it stood in solidarity with the people of the UAE and called for restraint and de-escalation across the region. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/06/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-oil-netanyahu-israel'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu: Netanyahu said Trump expressed appreciation for Israel’s help in rescuing a downed US crew member, publicly linking Israel to the operation’s aftermath. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/06/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-oil-netanyahu-israel'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/06/trump-threatens-to-destroy-iran-s-power-plants-and-bridges-over-hormuz-strait-closure'>Trump threatens to destroy Iran&#x27;s power plants and bridges over Hormuz Strait closure</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/06/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-oil-netanyahu-israel'>Middle East crisis live: Tehran warns Trump over strait of Hormuz threat; Netanyahu suggests Israel helped rescue downed US crew member</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/trump-threatens-tuesday-strikes-on-irans-power-plants-and-bridges-in-profanity-laden-post/'>Trump threatens Tuesday strikes on Iran&#x27;s power plants and bridges in profanity-laden post</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-issues-expletive-filled-threat-against-iran-as-details-of-u-s-aviators-rescue-emerge'>Trump issues expletive-filled threat against Iran as details of U.S. aviator&#x27;s rescue emerge</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988918/strait-of-hormuz-stays-sticking-point-as-ceasefire-remains-elusive'>Strait of Hormuz stays sticking point as ceasefire remains elusive</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-israel-war-whole-region-going-to-burn-iranian-parliament-speakers-warning-to-trump-11315145#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;Our Whole Region Is Going To Burn Because...&quot;: Iran On Trump&#x27;s Actions</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-gives-iran-until-tuesday-night-to-open-strait/'>Trump gives Iran until Tuesday night to open Strait</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='http